---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Us – 3rd/40th/41st Dublin, Donnybrook Scout Group"
  description="Founded in 1927, Donnybrook Scout Group (3rd/40th/41st Dublin) is one of the oldest continuously running Scout groups in Ireland, serving Dublin 4 and Dublin 6."
>
  <Hero
    title="About Our Group"
    subtitle="Founded in 1927 on Brookvale Road, Donnybrook, Dublin 4 — proudly wearing the Red Ties for nearly a century."
    eyebrow="Est. 1927 • Dublin 4 & Dublin 6"
    image="/images/hero-about.jpg"
    minHeight="360px"
  />

  <!-- Overview -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-overview grid grid-2">
        <div class="about-block">
          <span class="section-eyebrow">Who We Are</span>
          <h2>One of Ireland’s Oldest Scout Groups</h2>
          <p>
            Donnybrook Scout Group, 3rd/40th/41st Dublin, is a vibrant and active Scout Group based on
            Brookvale Road, Donnybrook, Dublin 4. We have approximately 200 members drawn from
            primarily Dublin 4 and 6 catchment areas.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our Group is a member of Scouting Ireland and in turn, the World Organisation of the
            Scouting Movement (WOSM).
          </p>
          <p>
            Our group has been mixed gender since the 1980s and is open to all, regardless of race,
            creed, age or ability.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="stats-panel">
          <div class="stat-item">
            <span class="stat-value">1927</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Year Founded in Donnybrook</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-item">
            <span class="stat-value">~200</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Active Youth &amp; Adult Members</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-item">
            <span class="stat-value">7</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Active Sections (Ages 6–26)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-item">
            <span class="stat-value">100th</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Centenary Celebrations Approaching</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- History & Governance -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container grid grid-2">
      <article class="card info-panel">
        <div class="card-body">
          <span class="section-eyebrow">Nearly a Century of Scouting</span>
          <h2>Our Group History</h2>
          <p>
            Our Group was founded in 1927 as one of the first scout troops of the then Catholic Boy
            Scouts of Ireland (CBSI). It is now one of the oldest established groups in Scouting
            Ireland, never once having closed its doors in over 95 years of continuous activity in
            the Dublin 4 community.
          </p>
          <p>
            While the “ethos” of the Scout Group has evolved over the decades, the principles of
            Scouting, and the promotion and informal education of young people through the Scout
            Method, continue to be our driving force as we look ahead to our 2027 Centenary.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card info-panel">
        <div class="card-body">
          <span class="section-eyebrow">Volunteer Led</span>
          <h2>Group Governance and Structure</h2>
          <p>
            Our Group comprises of 7 Sections (age groups) which meet weekly. Each Section is managed
            and run by a volunteer leader team, spearheaded by a Section Leader.
          </p>
          <p>
            Overseeing the Sections is Group Council, comprising of 7 Charity Trustees, as well as
            the Section Leaders and Youth Representatives. Group Council meets every two months.
          </p>
          <p>
            Supporting the day-to-day running of the Group is the Group Leader, an elected position
            with a 3 year term. The Group Leader is responsible for the overall planning and strategy
            of the Group, with the support of the Trustees and Group Council.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Historical Excerpt: All The Red Ties -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container history-essay">
      <blockquote class="history-quote">
        <p>
          The below is an excerpt from <strong>“All The Red Ties, Volume 1”</strong>, written by
          Dermot Lacey in commemoration of the Group’s 90th anniversary in 2017. Should anyone be
          interested in reading more, please{' '}
          <a href="/contact">contact the Group</a>.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <div class="essay-body">
        <p>
          The Sacred Heart Unit as it was officially called, of the new Association was established
          in 1927 by Monsignor Daniel Moloney P.P.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Unit began as one troop, the 3rd Dublin, with the first Scoutmaster, Charlie Fennell
          with Thomas Driver as his Assistant. Rapid growth saw the 40th and 41st quickly following
          in 1929. J.J. Walsh was first Scoutmaster of the 40th and Joseph Dempsey first of the
          41st. These were augmented in 1930 by Christy Keely, Pat Forde and John Mc Nulty. The
          Parish Priest of the day, Dean Dunne was the first President and E. Byrne and J. D’Arcy the
          first two Chairmen. The Macaoimh Gasra or Cub Scout Pack was also introduced in 1934.
          Showing true dedication these original team of Scout Masters were still in-situ five years
          later when they were joined by James P Buggle.
        </p>
        <p>
          There are a number of stories as to how the Unit got its numerical identification i.e. the
          3rd Dublin. The most common one related by a number of older members is that on the day of
          the launch of CBSI a delegate from Donnybrook Scouts was first in line at the entrance to
          the new Head Quarters on St. Stephen’s Green. When the door was opened he said he was there
          to register the new Troop. Not realizing that there was a rear entrance to the building he
          learned that he had been gazumped by two other troops and that the official number would
          now be the 3rd instead of the coveted 1st. The story goes on that because of his scarlet
          face on realising what had happened that the new Association awarded Donnybrook the scarlet
          or red neckerchief to commemorate his discomfiture. In turn, throughout the history of
          CBSI, Donnybrook allowed, or so we claim, the Chief Scout to wear our neckerchief – though
          legend tells us that National Head Quarters requested the Unit to change this during the
          1960’s – a request thankfully declined.
        </p>
        <p>
          According to Eugene Kirby, who was a Scoutmaster of the 41st in the 1940’s and 1950’s the
          numerical title was allocated because the Donnybrook Scout slipped on his way in to HQ
          letting the other two Scouts pass him by.
        </p>
        <p>
          The most likely account however is that prior to the formal establishment of CBSI there
          were already three other “Catholic” Scout Troops in existence in Dublin – the Dublin
          Catholic Arch Diocese that is – one in Fairview, one in Greystones and one other. When the
          new association issued its first charters, Fairview was allocated the title 1st Dublin,
          the Clarendon Street troop the number the 2nd Dublin and the remaining Troop deemed to be
          the HQ Troop. Donnybrook, as the first new CBSI established Troop, was allocated the
          number 3. This was followed in later years by the 40th and 41st. The Red Neckerchief
          which was granted to the new Troop was in honour of the Sacred Heart.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Gallery -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Through the Years</span>
        <h2>Moments From Our Group</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="gallery-grid">
        <div class="gallery-item">
          <img src="/images/about-1.jpg" alt="Donnybrook Scouts archive photo" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-item">
          <img src="/images/about-2.jpg" alt="Donnybrook Scout Group members" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-item">
          <img src="/images/scouts-hero.jpg" alt="Scouts outdoors" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-item">
          <img src="/images/about-3.jpg" alt="Group activity and camp" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-strip">
    <div class="container cta-strip-inner">
      <div>
        <h2>Become Part of the Story</h2>
        <p>Join one of our youth sections or volunteer as an adult leader in Donnybrook.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/join-us" class="btn btn-red btn-lg">Join Us</a>
        <a href="/sections" class="btn btn-outline-white btn-lg">Our Sections</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-overview {
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-block h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.15rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .stats-panel {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .stat-item {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--color-scout-red);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.15rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .stat-value {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .stat-label {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .info-panel h2 {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .history-essay {
    max-width: 840px;
  }

  .history-quote {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    padding: 1.35rem 1.65rem;
    background-color: var(--color-scout-red-soft);
    border-left: 5px solid var(--color-scout-red);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0;
  }

  .history-quote p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-darker);
  }

  .essay-body p {
    font-size: 1.03rem;
    line-height: 1.78;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .cta-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }
</style>
